Sun Nov  8 09:30:51 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Add soapy-plutosdr-libiio1-includedir.patch: search the
  include/iio/ header layout as well (libiio 1.x moved the
  headers there), fixing the CMake configure failure.
- Add soapy-plutosdr-libiio1-scan-api.patch: port the device
  scan to the libiio 1.x API (iio_scan, iio_err); the scan
  context API 0.2.4 uses was removed in libiio 1.0.
- Add soapy-plutosdr-libiio1-streaming.patch: port contexts,
  channel attrs and the streaming engine to the libiio 1.x
  block-queue API the driver needs to build at all.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Wed Oct 21 07:53:39 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.2.4:
  * Keep a bufflen buffer size across sample rate changes
  * Double the automatic RX buffer at 10.5 to 15.7 Msps, fixing
    sample loss at 13-15 Msps
  * Close remaining streams during device teardown, fixing a
    segfault when streams outlive the device

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Oct 11 09:23:54 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to version 0.2.3:
  * Scale TX streamer buffer with sample rate, fixing drops at high rates
  * Honor the bufflen stream kwarg and set the RX streamer MTU
  * Drop the device cache from device discovery
  * Make libusb support optional in cmake
  * Update for compat with newer CMake

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Aug 30 18:32:50 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Correct SPDX license to LGPL-2.1-only - upstream grants 2.1 only,
  there is no "or later" clause in any source file, README or
  debian/copyright
- Fix Source URL - GitHub archives by tag name, the old path 404s
- Declare pkgconfig(libiio) >= 0.9, the floor CMakeLists checks, so
  OBS holds the build rather than failing in configure
- Spec cleanup: drop Group tags, switch to %autosetup, wire up
  %check, normalise README.md line endings (shipped CRLF), drop
  stale "pro+" wording from the module description
- Explicitly require soapy-sdr: the automatic soname dependency pulls
  only libSoapySDR, so the module could be installed with no SoapySDR
  client - not even SoapySDRUtil - to reach it

